mode: "100644"
text: "# The WORDS framework — talk-content editing at the speed of text\n\nDescript's leverage is that the transcript IS the timeline — so the edit is a writing task, with two integrity\ngates unique to this tool (whose voice, whose meaning). Each letter is a gate; most edits fail at W (editing\naudio they should have edited as text) or the consent/meaning gates in O and the interview rule.\n\n## W — Write the edit\nTranscribe, run the **accuracy pass first** (names/jargon — errors become wrong edits and wrong captions), then\nedit like a document: cut tangents and bad takes, delete filler words + shorten silences in one Underlord step,\nrestructure by moving paragraphs. The discipline: **decide in text, verify by ear** — the transcript finds the\ncut fast, but the human listens to the actual audio before approving (pacing and tone don't live in text).\n\n## O — Overdub with consent\nFix flubs by typing — the correction regenerates in your **consent-verified, own-voice-only** clone.\n- **Craft limit:** single words and short phrases only; full paragraphs drift synthetic — re-record those.\n- **Practical limits:** ~24–48h training; lower-tier vocabulary caps; per-use credits (verify current).\n- **Integrity:** never clone anyone else's voice (Descript's verification blocks it by design — that's the\n  model); Overdub output is synthetic speech in a real voice, so honor AI-disclosure norms where they apply.\n\n## R — Refine the sound\n**Studio Sound** turns laptop audio near-studio in one click — run it **once per source file** (it costs credits\nper application, and cleaner audio also improves the transcript), not per revision. Level across speakers;\nshorten dead air; fix by re-take or Overdub-word, not by layering effects. Extreme noise is a re-record, not a\nrescue.\n\n## D — Dress the visuals\nFor video: **Automatic Multicam** cuts between speakers on separate tracks (record separate tracks on purpose);\ncaptions from the corrected transcript; B-roll where Underlord suggests and the human agrees; Eye Contact AI for\noff-camera reads (used honestly — a read is still a read); brand layout/templates from `design-and-templates`.\nDescript is not the place for beat-synced effects (→ `capcut`) or color finishing (→ Resolve/Premiere).\n\n## S — Ship the cuts\nOne recording → many assets, all from the same corrected transcript: the edited long-form export, AI-flagged\n**highlight clips** (Underlord flags; the **human picks** what represents people fairly), show notes, chapters,\na text post from the best exchange. Route clip-at-scale to `captions-and-clipping`/`opus-clip`, short-form\nstyling to `capcut`, the written cut to `text-post-and-microblog` — then `scheduling-and-queue` → **WoopSocial\npublishes** the finished files (it does not edit media).\n\n## The interview rule (runs through every letter)\nEditing someone else's words: **concision yes, meaning-flips never.** Text-editing makes it dangerously easy to\nrearrange a guest into saying something they didn't — preserve meaning, keep clip context, offer approval on\nsignificant edits, and let the human own the final cut of anyone else's words.\n"
